 understanding requires semantic analysis and reasoning over hour-scale vid=
eos, yet faces fundamental challenges:
incomplete coverage from lossy sampling, imprecise reasoning over long-rang=
e spatio-temporal interactions that flat representations
fail to capture, and imprecise localization of sparse evidence buried in ba=
ckground noise. Recent agentic approaches build searchable
caption databases for iterative querying, but the evidence space remains fu=
ndamentally unstructured=E2=80=94flat text and embeddings
cannot represent entity-level semantics or support traceable retrieval. We =
propose Scene Graph-Driven Agent (SGDAgent), which
restructures long video understanding by converting open-ended caption sear=
ch into structured candidate verification. Concretely, we
(i) design a hierarchical spatio-temporal scene graph structure for fine-gr=
ained video semantics representation, (ii) build a bottom-up
construction pipeline to generate such scene graphs, and (iii) design a sce=
ne graph-driven agent following a propose-verify-answer
paradigm with graph-based retrieval tools to search video content in a stru=
ctured way. Experiments across four benchmarks demonstrate substantial impr=
ovements: SGDAgent achieves +18.2 pp accuracy gain on LVBench with matched =
settings, and the structured
graph index enables lighter backbones to match stronger baselines.Agent tra=
jectory analysis confirms the gains stem from restructuring search itself=
